       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 2,550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day, which is three times the maximum daily dose. I can't think of a clinical situation where that dose is appropriate, and it carries a real risk of severe lactic acidosis. Confirming the same order doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter 850 mg PO TID with meals.** That is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **Enter a lower dose.** For example, 500 mg PO BID or TID with meals, to titrate up.\n- **Enter the order with a note** if there is a specific reason for the higher dose. I'd still suggest checking with your attending and pharmacy first, and I'd want the dose confirmed with them.\n\nIf 2,550 mg was meant as the daily total, tell me and I'll enter 850 mg TID right away."
      }
